  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "assistance-source-periods",
      "title": "Reading the assistance and coverage measures",
      "summary": "Reporting periods and denominators travel with every figure",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-distinct-measures",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Program receipt, program applications, health coverage and unemployment describe different populations. People may appear in several datasets. Their counts cannot be added into a single total of people receiving assistance.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-laus",
            "assist-census-insurance",
            "assist-ohio-heap",
            "assist-ohio-snap",
            "assist-ohio-medicaid",
            "assist-original-table10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-table10-period",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The original Table 10 labels SNAP, Medicaid and HEAP as 2025 but does not identify a month. This working edition supplies the actual selected sources and their periods: June 2025 SNAP, a Medicaid snapshot retrieved in February 2025, and the published 2024 HEAP county file. These are explicitly dated replacements for editorial review, not assumed reconstructions of an unspecified month.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-original-table10",
            "assist-ohio-snap",
            "assist-ohio-medicaid",
            "assist-ohio-heap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-uninsured-release",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The original statewide uninsured figure, 6.4%, matches the 2020–2024 five-year B27001 estimate. The separate 2024 one-year estimate is 6.7%. The original footnote’s one-year label therefore does not describe the numerical release used by that statewide figure. Both observations and both population denominators remain available.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-original-table10",
            "assist-census-insurance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-labour-vintage",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The original 2024 statewide unemployment rate of 4.3% matches the earlier 2024-benchmark release. The revised 2025-benchmark annual table reports 4.4% for the same 2024 measurement year. This is a source-vintage revision rather than an additional year of unemployment.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-original-table10",
            "assist-ohio-laus"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance-health",
      "title": "Health coverage across Ohio counties",
      "summary": "Civilian noninstitutionalized population · 2020–2024 ACS five-year",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-health-universe",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The denominator is the civilian noninstitutionalized population. It differs from the population for whom poverty status is determined. Uninsured counts here sum the eighteen disjoint no-coverage age/sex cells in B27001; percentages divide by the table’s total and round to one decimal.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-census-insurance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-health-uncertainty",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every original estimate and margin of error is retained with the source. The derived uninsured total does not carry a fabricated aggregate margin of error. County differences shown here are descriptive point estimates, without a claim of statistically significant ranking.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-census-insurance"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance-heap",
      "title": "Home energy assistance",
      "summary": "Published 2024 county applications and household shares",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-heap-label",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The downloaded government CSV labels its count “2024 HEAP Applications by County.” The accompanying housing-needs narrative calls the measure participating households. This edition preserves the downloaded measure label and explains that distinction; it does not infer approved benefits, payment amounts or unique household counts.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-heap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-heap-denominator",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The source context cites ACS five-year DP04 for household shares but does not identify the exact denominator release span. Published percentages remain unchanged. The source does not support reconstructing an exact denominator from a rounded percentage.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-heap"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance-snap",
      "title": "SNAP recipients and households",
      "summary": "June 2025 actual benefit receipt",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-snap-month",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "June 2025 PAMS records 1,388,233 active members in 711,651 households. The complete issuance-office rows, including unassigned recipients, reconcile to those statewide totals. The table describes benefit receipt in this month, rather than an annual average or a percentage of Ohio’s population.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-snap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-snap-geography",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The source includes combined Def/Paudling and South Central offices. Their values remain together and are not distributed across counties. County-looking labels therefore describe reporting offices, with combined and unassigned rows clearly marked.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-snap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-snap-age",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "PAMS defines SNAP adults as over age 22 and children as under age 22 who live with a parent. Those are the received source’s words and boundary convention. These counts must not be relabeled as the under-18 child population used in poverty or food-insecurity datasets.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-snap"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance-medicaid",
      "title": "Medicaid county enrollment snapshot",
      "summary": "Retrieved February 19, 2025 · population from 2019–2023 ACS",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-medicaid-source",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The county table is HPIO’s analysis of the Ohio Department of Medicaid dashboard and Census population. The source gives a retrieval date of February 19, 2025 and a February 2025 publication, but does not name the enrollment month. This edition retains that exact distinction.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-medicaid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-medicaid-revision",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "ODM dashboard values can be updated for retroactive and back-dated eligibility. The published total-population denominator is the 2023 ACS five-year estimate, covering 2019–2023. Expansion enrollees are part of all Medicaid enrollment; those two columns overlap and must not be added.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-medicaid"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assistance-labour",
      "title": "Unemployment: same year, two releases",
      "summary": "2024 annual averages · original and revised benchmarks",
      "breakBefore": true,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "assist-labour-definition",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Unemployment rates use the civilian labour force as their denominator. The annual estimates are by residence and are not seasonally adjusted. Published counts are rounded to the nearest 100; the provider calculates its rate using unrounded estimates. Consequently the printed rounded counts need not reproduce the published rate exactly.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-laus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "assist-labour-release",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each row retains both the original release dated April 22, 2025 and the revised release dated May 5, 2026. The rate difference is current minus original in percentage points. Both columns measure 2024, so their difference is not a time trend.",
          "sourceIds": [
            "assist-ohio-laus"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
